libvips (through @img/sharp-libvips-* and sharp)
------------------------------------------------
@infrabyx/connectors' MEDIA adapter `sharp` loads libvips through the npm package `sharp`
(Apache-2.0, https://github.com/lovell/sharp). On each platform sharp installs a prebuilt
`@img/sharp-libvips-<platform>` package that contains libvips and its dependencies as shared
libraries.

  Component:  libvips (https://www.libvips.org/, https://github.com/libvips/libvips)
  Package:    @img/sharp-libvips-<platform>, version 1.3.4 (with sharp 0.35.5)
  Licence:    GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or later (LGPL-3.0-or-later),
              https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html
  Source:     https://github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips (build scripts and the versions of every
              bundled library), https://github.com/libvips/libvips (libvips source)

The binaries are used unmodified and loaded dynamically at run time. They are never modified,
vendored into this repository or statically linked into Infrabyx code; a user may replace them
with their own build of libvips, as the LGPL allows (see https://sharp.pixelplumbing.com/install
"Custom libvips"). The licence exception covers this package family only (owner decision,
OWNER-QUESTIONS #53, docs/DECISIONS.md PL5-D-11).
